      "sex": null,
      "dx_date_min": "2018-01-01",
      "dx_date_max": null
    },
    "text": "The EPITHELIAL LAYER contains no blood vessels or lymphatics",
    "codes": null,
    "notes": null
  },
  {
    "rule_id": "summary_stage_2018:bladder_renal_pelvis_and_ureters_anatomic_structures:bladder_renal_pelvis_and:d3",
    "source_doc": "summary_stage_2018",
    "section_path": [
      "URINARY SYSTEM",
      "BLADDER, RENAL PELVIS AND URETERS ANATOMIC STRUCTURES"
    ],
    "anchor": "L10107-L10149:bladder-renal-pelvis-and-ureters-anatomic-structures",
    "kind": "definition",
    "item_ids": [
      764
    ],
    "applies_to": {
      "sites": null,
      "histologies": null,
      "behaviors": null,
      "sex": null,
      "dx_date_min": "2018-01-01",
      "dx_date_max": null
    },
    "text": "The BASEMENT MEMBRANE, a sheet of extracellular material, functions as a filtration barrier\n\nand a boundary involved in generating and maintaining tissue structure",
    "codes": null,
    "notes": null
  },
  {
    "rule_id": "summary_stage_2018:bladder_renal_pelvis_and_ureters_anatomic_structures:bladder_renal_pelvis_and:d4",
    "source_doc": "summary_stage_2018",
    "section_path": [
      "URINARY SYSTEM",
      "BLADDER, RENAL PELVIS AND URETERS ANATOMIC STRUCTURES"
    ],
    "anchor": "L10107-L10149:bladder-renal-pelvis-and-ureters-anatomic-structures",
    "kind": "definition",
    "item_ids": [
      764
    ],
    "applies_to": {
      "sites": null,
      "histologies": null,
      "behaviors": null,
      "sex": null,
      "dx_date_min": "2018-01-01",
      "dx_date_max": null
    },
    "text": "The LAMINA PROPRIA, composed of areolar connective tissue, contains blood vessels, nerves,\n\nand, in some regions, glands. Once tumor has broken through the basement membrane into the lamina propria, it can spread by way of the lymphatics and blood vessels to other parts of the body",
    "codes": null,
    "notes": null
  },
  {
    "rule_id": "summary_stage_2018:bladder_renal_pelvis_and_ureters_anatomic_structures:bladder_renal_pelvis_and:d5",
    "source_doc": "summary_stage_2018",
    "section_path": [
      "URINARY SYSTEM",
      "BLADDER, RENAL PELVIS AND URETERS ANATOMIC STRUCTURES"
    ],
    "anchor": "L10107-L10149:bladder-renal-pelvis-and-ureters-anatomic-structures",
    "kind": "definition",
    "item_ids": [
      764
    ],
    "applies_to": {
      "sites": null,
      "histologies": null,
      "behaviors": null,
      "sex": null,
      "dx_date_min": "2018-01-01",
      "dx_date_max": null
    },
    "text": "The urinary sites do NOT have a MUSCULARIS MUCOSAE, and, therefore, the lamina propria\n\nand the submucosa are difficult to separate. These terms are used interchangeably",
    "codes": null,
    "notes": null
  },
  {
    "rule_id": "summary_stage_2018:bladder_renal_pelvis_and_ureters_anatomic_structures:bladder_renal_pelvis_and:d6",
    "source_doc": "summary_stage_2018",
    "section_path": [
      "URINARY SYSTEM",
      "BLADDER, RENAL PELVIS AND URETERS ANATOMIC STRUCTURES"
    ],
    "anchor": "L10107-L10149:bladder-renal-pelvis-and-ureters-anatomic-structures",
    "kind": "definition",
    "item_ids": [
      764
    ],
    "applies_to": {
      "sites": null,
      "histologies": null,
      "behaviors": null,
      "sex": null,
      "dx_date_min": "2018-01-01",
      "dx_date_max": null
    },
    "text": "The SUBMUCOSA is a thick layer of either dense or areolar connective tissue. It contains blood\n\nvessels, lymphatic vessels, nerves, and, in some regions, glands",
    "codes": null,
    "notes": null
  },
  {
    "rule_id": "summary_stage_2018:bladder_renal_pelvis_and_ureters_anatomic_structures:bladder_renal_pelvis_and:d7",
    "source_doc": "summary_stage_2018",
    "section_path": [
      "URINARY SYSTEM",
      "BLADDER, RENAL PELVIS AND URETERS ANATOMIC STRUCTURES"
    ],
    "anchor": "L10107-L10149:bladder-renal-pelvis-and-ureters-anatomic-structures",
    "kind": "definition",
    "item_ids": [
      764
    ],
    "applies_to": {
      "sites": null,
      "histologies": null,
      "behaviors": null,
      "sex": null,
      "dx_date_min": "2018-01-01",
      "dx_date_max": null
    },
    "text": "The MUSCULARIS PROPRIA is composed of multiple layers of muscle tissue; it constitutes the\n\nwall of the organ",
    "codes": null,
    "notes": null
  },
  {
    "rule_id": "summary_stage_2018:bladder_renal_pelvis_and_ureters_anatomic_structures:bladder_renal_pelvis_and:d8",
    "source_doc": "summary_stage_2018",
    "section_path": [
      "URINARY SYSTEM",
      "BLADDER, RENAL PELVIS AND URETERS ANATOMIC STRUCTURES"
    ],
    "anchor": "L10107-L10149:bladder-renal-pelvis-and-ureters-anatomic-structures",
    "kind": "definition",
    "item_ids": [
      764
    ],
    "applies_to": {
      "sites": null,
      "histologies": null,
      "behaviors": null,
      "sex": null,
      "dx_date_min": "2018-01-01",
      "dx_date_max": null
    },
    "text": "The SEROSA, the outermost layer covering, is a serous membrane, part of the visceral\n\nperitoneum. It covers only the superior surface of the bladder. There is no serosa on the renal pelvis or ureters.",
    "codes": null,
    "notes": null
  },
  {
    "rule_id": "summary_stage_2018:bladder_renal_pelvis_and_ureters_anatomic_structures:bladder_renal_pelvis_and:d9",
    "source_doc": "summary_stage_2018",
    "section_path": [
      "URINARY SYSTEM",
      "BLADDER, RENAL PELVIS AND URETERS ANATOMIC STRUCTURES"
    ],
    "anchor": "L10107-L10149:bladder-renal-pelvis-and-ureters-anatomic-structures",
    "kind": "definition",
    "item_ids": [
      764
    ],
    "applies_to": {
      "sites": null,
      "histologies": null,
      "behaviors": null,
      "sex": null,
      "dx_date_min": "2018-01-01",
      "dx_date_max": null
    },
    "text": "Where there is no serosa, the connective tissue of surrounding structures merges with\n\nthe connective tissue of the urinary organs and is called ADVENTITIA.",
    "codes": null,
    "notes": null
  }
]
